== Unit tests (Lune)

Catch.spec.luau
  ok    every species table sums to 1 and matches req. 5 within 0.01 percentage points
  ok    200,000 rolls of the Sea Fog table match its odds (the server's pick function)
  ok    ring mode and bite wait follow the weather; the storm fishes as Storm at the eye only
  ok    size roll: clamp 0.5-3.0, mean 1.00, median about 0.97, about 4% at 1.5x or more (sheet §9.3)
  ok    marks: Drizzled 20% of Showers catches, Misty 15% of Sea Fog, none in Clear or the storm
  ok    value = base x size x mark x 1.14^Rod, nearest whole coin, at least 1
  ok    the first catch pays 12 and makes the Rod affordable on the second catch, whatever it is
  ok    ring steps by tier per mode (req. 3.4)
  ok    a bite payload carries the tier but never the species, size or mark; fog has no ring yet

Config.spec.luau
  ok    species ids are unique, tiers exist, pools are known, weights and values are positive
  ok    one free zone (Pebble Cove) and the layout uses it
  ok    products and passes have unique keys; every id is 0 so nothing can be bought
  ok    onboarding steps are numbered 1..n without gaps and use known guides
  ok    client-to-server remotes all declare rate limits; the fishing limits are the brief's
  ok    the weather timetable covers the whole cycle without gaps and names every spot

Data.spec.luau
  ok    new profiles are independent deep copies
  ok    reconcile fills missing fields of old saves
  ok    migration steps run in order and bump the version
